  <section id="visibility">
    <h2>Visibility and Safety on the Water</h2>
    <p>
      When swimming in active waterways where kayakers or paddleboarders might be present, you must be seen. A high-visibility tow float wild swimming setup is non-negotiable.
    </p>
    <p>
      A tow float trails behind you on a short leash, providing a bright visual marker for other water users. Many models also double as waterproof dry bags, allowing you to safely store your car keys or phone while you swim. [Source: Royal Life Saving Society UK]
    </p>
